Here is an example of a new CSS style for a button element:

```css
button {
  background-color: #4CAF50; /* Green */
  border: none;
  color: white;
  padding: 15px 32px;
  text-align: center;
  text-decoration: none;
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 16px;
  margin: 4px 2px;
  cursor: pointer;
  border-radius: 12px;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #3e8e41;
}
```

In this example, the button has a green background with white text, no border, and rounded corners. The size, padding, and margin are also specified. Additionally, there is a hover effect that changes the background color to a darker shade of green when the user hovers over the button.
